msgid "geopedia.lever_arm.title"
msgstr "Lever arm"

msgid "geopedia.lever_arm.example"
msgstr "The sensor is offset from the vehicle origin. A 0.10 m error in the estimated lever arm produces a 0.10 m error without rotation."

msgid "geopedia.lever_arm.unit_effect"
msgstr "Metres in the body frame; attitude rotates this vector before adding it to the trajectory position."

msgid "geopedia.lever_arm.model_limit"
msgstr "Physical and estimated mounts are separate. Knowing the slot does not reveal the correct mount to processing."

msgid "geopedia.boresight.title"
msgstr "Boresight: mounting orientation"

msgid "geopedia.boresight.example"
msgstr "In the workshop passes, fit the relative sensor-to-body orientation using shared surfaces."

msgid "geopedia.boresight.unit_effect"
msgstr "Radians; at 100 m, a 0.001 rad angular error causes approximately 0.10 m of lateral displacement."

msgid "geopedia.boresight.model_limit"
msgstr "The workshop requires at least three nonparallel planes to observe the full adjustment. A low residual on one plane does not guarantee full calibration."

msgid "geopedia.time_sync.title"
msgstr "Time synchronization"

msgid "geopedia.time_sync.example"
msgstr "A 0.02 s sensor-to-trajectory offset at 10 m/s shifts a point by approximately 0.20 m."

msgid "geopedia.time_sync.unit_effect"
msgstr "Seconds; processing queries the pose at sensor time plus the estimated offset and interpolates position and attitude."

msgid "geopedia.time_sync.model_limit"
msgstr "Returns outside the trajectory interval are invalid. Constant speed alone cannot separate time offset from a longitudinal lever arm."

msgid "geopedia.imu_ins.title"
msgstr "IMU and inertial navigation"

msgid "geopedia.imu_ins.example"
msgstr "In the navigation domain, the gyroscope integrates attitude and observed acceleration drives the position and velocity filter through GNSS outages."

msgid "geopedia.imu_ins.unit_effect"
msgstr "Acceleration in m/s² and rotation in rad/s; bias and random walk accumulate drift. Game local gravity: 9.80665 m/s²."

msgid "geopedia.imu_ins.model_limit"
msgstr "The teaching filter has six translational states and complementary attitude; it is not a full commercial INS. The city connects an observed diagnostic; photos and cloud still use ideal poses."

msgid "geopedia.dmi_zupt.title"
msgstr "DMI and zero-velocity update"

msgid "geopedia.dmi_zupt.example"
msgstr "DMI observes longitudinal speed. ZUPT uses a sensor-confirmed stop to update zero velocity."

msgid "geopedia.dmi_zupt.unit_effect"
msgstr "DMI in m/s; wet roads multiply its longitudinal variance by 25. ZUPT requires 2 s with speed <0.05 m/s, rotation <0.01 rad/s and gravity difference <0.1 m/s²."

msgid "geopedia.dmi_zupt.model_limit"
msgstr "A visually stopped vehicle is insufficient: without enough observed evidence the filter does not apply ZUPT. DMI also has scale error and slip."

msgid "geopedia.base_rtk_ppk.title"
msgstr "Base, DGNSS, RTK and PPK"

msgid "geopedia.base_rtk_ppk.example"
msgstr "Install a base on a known mark to correct common error. PPK reapplies the time-stamped base log to the office product."

msgid "geopedia.base_rtk_ppk.unit_effect"
msgstr "In the RTK model: sky openness ≥0.4 permits float; ≥0.7 for 10 s and a base within 2 km permit fix, with a compatible profile and available corrections."

msgid "geopedia.base_rtk_ppk.model_limit"
msgstr "No RF carrier simulation. The base does not remove local multipath. PPK requires compatible logs and is never a live GNSS state. Without a connected base, the city reports autonomous GNSS."

msgid "geopedia.lidar_density.title"
msgstr "LiDAR: density and coverage"

msgid "geopedia.lidar_density.example"
msgstr "QC counts distinct valid returns per support cell. Merging the same batch again does not increase density."

msgid "geopedia.lidar_density.unit_effect"
msgstr "Points/m² over clipped useful area; LiDAR products use 1×1 m cells. The contract defines the target density and required cell fraction."

msgid "geopedia.lidar_density.model_limit"
msgstr "The coloured city cloud is a bounded sampled preview. Its visible count, nominal rate and LOD do not measure official product density."

msgid "geopedia.lidar_occlusion.title"
msgstr "LiDAR: occlusion and passes"

msgid "geopedia.lidar_occlusion.example"
msgstr "A facade or vehicle can hide the required surface. Another pass with a different line of sight can fill the gap."

msgid "geopedia.lidar_occlusion.unit_effect"
msgstr "Coverage is observed useful area divided by required area. High density in one part does not compensate for an unobserved area."

msgid "geopedia.lidar_occlusion.model_limit"
msgstr "The preview does not certify completeness. Octrees, chunks and LOD representatives speed queries and drawing; QC still uses original samples."

msgid "geopedia.lidar_returns.title"
msgstr "LiDAR: multiple returns"

msgid "geopedia.lidar_returns.example"
msgstr "In transmissive vegetation, one pulse can reach multiple surfaces. Return number identifies the order within a pulse."

msgid "geopedia.lidar_returns.unit_effect"
msgstr "The simulator permits up to three returns and stops below 0.1 energy, beyond range or at an opaque surface."

msgid "geopedia.lidar_returns.model_limit"
msgstr "This is a discrete material-and-energy model without a full waveform. The city preview does not establish multiple-return vegetation acquisition."

msgid "geopedia.rmse.title"
msgstr "RMSE and independent checks"

msgid "geopedia.rmse.example"
msgstr "Compare estimated positions with independent check references. Points used in adjustment do not replace checkpoints."

msgid "geopedia.rmse.unit_effect"
msgstr "Absolute RMSE in metres: square root of the mean squared 3D distances. The game requires at least three matches and distribution across the area."

msgid "geopedia.rmse.model_limit"
msgstr "Without sufficient matches the result is insufficient, never zero. Filter sigma and inter-pass residual are not the same as absolute RMSE."

msgid "geopedia.camera_calibration.title"
msgstr "Camera calibration"

msgid "geopedia.camera_calibration.example"
msgstr "On the bench, observe a known grid in at least three distinct poses and reserve another pose for validation."

msgid "geopedia.camera_calibration.unit_effect"
msgstr "Intrinsics fx, fy, cx and cy are in pixels; k1 and k2 describe normalized radial distortion. The solver minimizes reprojection residuals."

msgid "geopedia.camera_calibration.model_limit"
msgstr "Pinhole model with two radial terms. A low residual on the fitted grid does not replace independent validation or mounting calibration."

msgid "geopedia.historical_geodesy.title"
msgstr "Survey marks and historical geodesy"

msgid "geopedia.historical_geodesy.example"
msgstr "Zero Stone and Clock Tower connect the São Datum network to position and height references. Verify a displaced mark before using it as control."

msgid "geopedia.historical_geodesy.unit_effect"
msgstr "Coordinates and heights in metres need a declared reference. The game separates a mark’s catalogued coordinate from its physical position."

msgid "geopedia.historical_geodesy.model_limit"
msgstr "São Datum and its history are fictional; the local system has no EPSG code. The network is not a historical reconstruction of a real survey."

msgid "geopedia.trajectory_drift.title"
msgstr "Trajectory drift and uncertainty"

msgid "geopedia.trajectory_drift.example"
msgstr "During GNSS outages the filter propagates position, velocity and covariance. New observations can constrain uncertainty growth."

msgid "geopedia.trajectory_drift.unit_effect"
msgstr "Position sigma in metres; 3D sigma is the square root of the sum of the three component variances. GNSS solution age is in seconds."

msgid "geopedia.trajectory_drift.model_limit"
msgstr "σ is model uncertainty, not error measured against truth. City diagnostics use observations and retain a bounded trail; this trajectory does not replace product georeferencing."

msgid "geopedia.territory_attention.title"
msgstr "Territory attention"

msgid "geopedia.territory_attention.example"
msgstr "Active capture attracts attention in a zone; disguise and Calm City change the response. The map shows values from each territory tracker."

msgid "geopedia.territory_attention.unit_effect"
msgstr "Score from 0 to 100; levels change at 20, 40, 60, 80 and 100. Actions have a minimum 30 s cooldown and at least 3 s warning."

msgid "geopedia.territory_attention.model_limit"
msgstr "Score is not an action in progress. Calm City or a calm contract suppresses hostile actions even if recorded attention remains."

